<title>MEXICO: Mexico's 28-day Cetes rate rises in auction.</title>
<headline>Mexico's 28-day Cetes rate rises in auction.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1996-10-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico's 28-day Cetes rate rose in this week's primary auction and demand fell, Banco de Mexico said.</p>
<p>Auction results were: (all rates in percent)</p>
<p>Maturity    Weighted Avg   Change (bps)  Min Rate  Max Rate</p>
<p>28-Day	25.90	    -316	    25.90     25.90</p>
<p>91-Day	28.75	    -364	    27.75     28.98</p>
<p>182-Day     29.05	    -221	    28.50     29.17</p>
<p>350-Day     28.65				28.25     28.77</p>
<p>Last week the 357-day paper was assigned at 26.83 pct.</p>
<p>Maturity    Assigned	  Demand		Bid/Cover</p>
<p>28-Day	900 million pesos   3.050 bln pesos    3.39</p>
<p>91-Day	900 million pesos   2.240 bln pesos    2.49</p>
<p>182-Day     900 million pesos   3.847 bln pesos    4.27</p>
<p>350-Day     600 million pesos   3.546 bln pesos    5.91</p>
<p>The bid-to-cover ratio for the auction as a whole was 3.84 compared with 4.34 the week before, on demand of 14.34 billion pesos the week before.</p>
<p>Details were as follows:</p>
<p>    28-Day			  nil basis points</p>
<p>    91-Day			  23  basis points</p>
<p>    182-Day			 12  basis points</p>
<p>    350-Day			 12  basis points</p>
<p>-- Mexico City newsroom, 525 728-9559.</p>
</text>
